 The qualified observer evaluated here is a causal RKF-IMU estimator that uses the six-axis accelerometer and gyroscope measurements exclusively. Across the six deterministic closed-loop routes used in RQ1, it achieved a mean scheduled-grade MAE of 1.18210$^{\circ}$. All 62582 logged observer updates were valid, and no constraint violation, solver failure, or timeout was recorded. The same observer is used as the standalone scheduling source in RQ1; fusion-specific calibration and inference are considered separately below.
 
-Figure~\ref{fig:imu_observer_trace} shows the complete 5201-sample, 52-s P2 Sharp-turn transition record obtained by evaluating both estimator branches within the same closed-loop simulation. After excluding the initial 0.5~s, the raw grade-estimation MAE was 1.00461$^{\circ}$ for the qualified observer and 0.62075$^{\circ}$ for ModernTCN-delta. With a 0.1$^{\circ}$ tolerance for a decisive local difference, the qualified observer had lower absolute error on 34.07\% of the evaluated samples, ModernTCN-delta had lower error on 55.95\%, and the remaining 9.98\% were near ties.
+Figure~\ref{fig:imu_observer_trace} shows the complete 5201-sample, 52-s P2 Sharp-turn transition record obtained by evaluating both estimator branches within the same closed-loop simulation. After excluding the initial 0.5~s, the raw grade-estimation MAE was 0.22563$^{\circ}$ for the qualified observer and 0.62075$^{\circ}$ for ModernTCN-delta. With a 0.1$^{\circ}$ tolerance for a decisive local difference, the qualified observer had lower absolute error on 53.54\% of the evaluated samples, ModernTCN-delta had lower error on 25.28\%, and the remaining 21.18\% were near ties.
 
 The qualified observer evaluated here is a causal RKF-IMU estimator that uses the six-axis accelerometer and gyroscope measurements exclusively. Across the six deterministic closed-loop routes used in RQ1, it achieved a mean scheduled-grade MAE of 1.18210$^{\circ}$. All 62582 logged observer updates were valid, and no constraint violation, solver failure, or timeout was recorded. The same observer is used as the standalone scheduling source in RQ1; fusion-specific calibration and inference are considered separately below.
 
